# What is Data Science?

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Data</strong> is any form of organized information. This could be words, numbers or pictures.</p>

<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;"><strong>📖 Data Science </strong> is the process of making meaning from that data.</p>

</div>

#### Learning data science helps students develop critical thinking skills and understand how to make informed decisions based on evidence. It teaches students how to gather information, look for patterns, ask questions, and use data to support conclusions.

#### Data science is used across many fields. It helps organizations solve problems, improve efficiency, and make predictions about the future. By studying data science, students gain skills that prepare them for a wide range of careers and help them better understand how the world works.

#### Many industries rely on data science to make decisions and innovate. The examples below show how different fields use data to improve their work.

